Somehow I seem to have been disconnected from the
LaTeX-3 discussion list recently, so apologies in advance
if this has been answered recently, but ...
nfss2 has been "withdrawn" from the CTAN servers.
This package contained modified versions of
AMS files which could (with a little effort) be made
to work with LaTeX-2e.  Does anybody have (hacked)
versions of the AMS files (especially, amsart.sty) which
they would be willing to share?

I know the AMS intends to release new versions
later this year - perhaps to coincide with the
official release of LaTeX-2e, but it would be nice
to have a working version now.

